<h1 class="main-title">Maakeh [Rooftop Railing] and the Protection of the Soul</h1>
<h2 class="sub-title">Halacha 2</h2>
<div class="source-ref">Likutay Halachos · Choshen Mishpat, Part II &nbsp;|&nbsp; In Hilchos Chovel B'chaveiro [Laws of One Who Injures His Fellow], Halacha 3</div>

<p>The matter of the commandment of <span class="kt">maakeh</span> [rooftop railing] and the protection of the soul of Israel — to save him from all manner of harm — as it is written in the <em>Shulchan Aruch</em> [Code of Jewish Law]:</p>

<p>Based on what <span class="kt">Rabainu</span> [our master, teacher, and Rebbe — Rebbe Nachman of Breslov], of blessed memory, wrote on the verse: <em>"And Yaakov traveled to Sukos and built himself a house, and for his livestock he made sukos [booths]"</em> [Bereishis 33:17] — in §266 [of Likutay Moharan, Part I] and so forth. See there.</p>

<p>And the general principle is: that through the commandment of <span class="kt">sukkah</span> [booth] one is able to build a house — for the <em>sukkah</em> is the aspect of intellect [<span class="kt">seichel</span>] and wisdom — the aspect of <em>"the mother [<span class="kt">Ima</span>] who spreads her shelter [<span class="kt">m'sacheches</span>] over the children [<span class="kt">banin</span>]"</em> [Zohar III:103a] — the aspect of: <em>"call to understanding 'mother'"</em> [Mishlei 7:4]. And through this specifically one can build oneself a house — in the aspect of: <em>"By wisdom a house is built..."</em> [Mishlei 24:3] and so forth. See there.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the commandment of <em>maakeh</em> for one's house — as it is written: <em>"When you build a new house, you shall make a railing for your roof, and you shall not place blood in your house, for the one who falls shall fall from it"</em> [Devarim 22:8]. For when one builds a new house — then one must build one's house with wisdom and so forth, as stated above. And therefore the essential building of the house is through the commandment of <em>sukkah</em>, as stated above. And therefore one must make a <em>maakeh</em> for one's house — in order to save and to guard the souls of Israel so that they should not be harmed, G‑d forbid. And this is the aspect of <em>sukkah</em> — the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter over the children"</em> — for Hashem, Blessed be He, watches over His people Israel. And the essential protection is through the aspect of <em>sukkah</em> — the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter over the children"</em> — that is, as it were, the <span class="kt">Shechina</span> [Divine Presence] shelters and spreads her canopy over the children of Israel, to guard them and to save them from all manner of harm — as we request in the blessing of <em>Hashkiveinu</em> [the night prayer]: <em>"And spread over us the sukkah of Your peace..."</em> and so forth, and <em>"...Guard our going out..."</em> and so forth — for the essential protection is through the aspect of <em>sukkah</em> — the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter over the children,"</em> as stated above.</p>

<p>And likewise Hashem, Blessed be He, commanded us — upon each and every one of Israel — that one should always strive to guard and to save the souls of Israel from all manner of harm. For we are obligated to walk in His ways, Blessed be He — as it is written: <em>"And you shall walk in His ways"</em> [Devarim 28:9]. And therefore we too are obligated — each one — to guard and to save the souls of Israel from all manner of harm. And through our fulfilling this commandment — namely, the commandment of guarding the soul of Israel — through this we arouse the same dimension above as well: that Hashem, Blessed be He, will also guard us and shelter and spread His canopy over us — in the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter over the children,"</em> as stated above.</p>

<p>It emerges that this commandment of guarding the soul of Israel is in the aspect of <em>sukkah</em> — the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter..."</em> and so forth, as stated above. And therefore the Torah commanded this essential commandment specifically at the time when one builds one's house — namely, the commandment of <em>maakeh</em> for one's house, which is for the sake of protecting the soul of Israel so that one should not be harmed. For specifically at the time of building one's house one must strive to engage in this commandment of protecting the soul — for through making a <em>maakeh</em> and guarding the souls of Israel so that they should not be harmed, G‑d forbid — and this is the aspect of <em>sukkah</em> — the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter over the children,"</em> as stated above — through this specifically one is able to build one's house. For the essential building of the house is through the aspect of <em>sukkah</em>, as stated above. And through the commandment of <em>maakeh</em> — which is for the sake of protecting souls from harm — through this one fulfills the aspect of <em>sukkah</em> — the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter over the children,"</em> as stated above. And through this specifically one can build a house — in the aspect of: <em>"And Yaakov traveled to Sukos and built himself a house"</em> [Bereishis 33:17], as stated above — for the <em>sukkah</em> is the aspect of intellect, as stated above. And through this the essential building of the house — in the aspect of: <em>"By wisdom a house is built"</em> [Mishlei 24:3], as stated above.</p>

<p>And the essential protection from harm is through the intellect — as we have already written several times — for through the wholeness of the intellect all manner of harm is nullified — in the aspect of: <em>"They shall neither harm nor destroy, for the earth will be filled with the knowledge of [G‑d]..."</em> [Yeshaya 11:9].</p>

<p>It emerges that when one makes a <em>maakeh</em> and guards against harm — this is the aspect of the wholeness of <span class="kt">da'as</span> [knowledge / inner awareness / mind]. For when harm comes upon one, G‑d forbid, this is the aspect of a defect of <em>da'as</em>, as is brought in another place. But protection from harm through the commandment of <em>maakeh</em> — this is the aspect of the wholeness of <em>da'as</em> — the aspect of <em>sukkah</em> — the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter over the children"</em> — to guard them from all manner of harm. And through this the essential building of the house — in the aspect of: <em>"By wisdom a house is built,"</em> as stated above.</p>

<p>And therefore the Torah commanded: <em>"When you build a new house"</em> — that is, when you wish to engage in the building of the house — then you must draw the aspect of <em>sukkah</em>, the aspect of the wholeness of <em>da'as</em>, in the aspect of: <em>"By wisdom a house is built,"</em> as stated above. And therefore: <em>"and you shall make a railing for your roof"</em> — in order to guard the souls of Israel. And through this the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter over the children"</em> — the aspect of <em>sukkah</em> — is drawn. And through this the essential building, as stated above.</p>

<p><em>"And you shall not place blood in your house"</em> — for the dominance of blood is the opposite of intellect — for the dominance of blood is the aspect of anger [<span class="kt">ka'as</span>], from which come all the harms. For from it comes the spirit of foolishness [<span class="kt">ruach shtus</span>] of all the sins that come from the dominance of blood, as is brought in another place. And they are the aspect of the spirit of animality [<span class="kt">ruach ha'behemiyus</span>], which is the opposite of the aspect of <em>sukkah</em> — as is explained in the aforementioned Torah [Likutay Moharan I, §266]. See there.</p>

<p>And therefore when you build your house — you must draw intellect, the aspect of <em>sukkah</em>, through the commandment of <em>maakeh</em>, as stated above — for through this the essential building of the house, as stated above. <em>"And you shall not place blood in your house"</em> specifically — that is, <span class="repeat-bracket">[for you must draw intellect, the aspect of <em>sukkah</em>, through the commandment of <em>maakeh</em>, as stated above — for through this the essential building of the house, as stated above.]</span> And you shall not place blood in your house specifically — that is, for you must guard yourself that your house should not cause harm, G‑d forbid — for this is the corruption of the house. For harm is a defect of <em>da'as</em> — through which comes the corruption of the house — for the essential [purpose of the] house is through wisdom, as stated above.</p>

<p>And this is: <em>"for the one who falls shall fall from it"</em> — for we must guard the souls of Israel in order to draw the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter over the children"</em> — in order to raise up the fallen <span class="kt">Sukkas Dovid ha'nofeles</span> [the fallen Sukkah of David]. For when one of Israel falls and is harmed, G‑d forbid — physically or spiritually, G‑d forbid — then, as it were, there is pain to the <em>Shechina</em>, as is known. And then the <em>Shechina</em>, G‑d forbid, is in the aspect of <em>"the fallen Sukkah of David"</em> [Amos 9:11]. And conversely — when one guards a soul of Israel from falling and from harm — then, as it were, one sustains the <em>Shechina</em> from its falling — in the aspect of: <em>"I will raise up the fallen Sukkah of David"</em> [Amos 9:11]. For the <em>Shechina</em> is always with Israel, as is known — for guarding the soul of Israel is the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter over the children,"</em> and through this one raises up the fallen Sukkah of David. And this is the aspect of <em>maakeh</em>, as stated above — so that the one who falls should not fall — for then it is, G‑d forbid, the aspect of the fallen Sukkah of David. Therefore one must make a <em>maakeh</em> in order to be guarded from this — and then the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter"</em> and so forth is drawn, as stated above. And then it is fulfilled: <em>"I will raise up the fallen Sukkah of David"</em> — speedily in our days,</p>

<div class="closing-amein">Amen.</div>

<div class="blessed-line">Blessed is Hashem forever, Amen and Amen.</div>

<p>All of this is related to the above.</p>

<p>And see in the aforementioned Torah [Likutay Moharan I, §266] the matter of <em>sukkah</em> — that it is the aspect of intellect [<em>seichel</em>] — the aspect of the boundary of a human being [<em>geider ha'adam</em>], the opposite of the boundary of an animal [<em>geider ha'behema</em>], which is the absence of <em>da'as</em>. And this is: <em>"and you shall not place blood in your house"</em> — for the dominance of blood is the aspect of animality — the aspect of the spirit of foolishness [<em>ruach shtus</em>] that comes from the dominance of blood, as is understood in another place — which is the opposite of the aspect of <em>sukkah</em>, as stated above. And they corrupt the house, as stated above.</p>

<p>And see in <em>Etz Chaim</em> [the Kabbalistic work of the Ari, Rabbi Yitzchak Luria] in the chapter <em>Sha'ar ABIY"A</em> [<span class="kt">Atzilus, Beriya, Yetzira, Asiya</span> — the four spiritual worlds: Emanation, Creation, Formation, Action] regarding the matter of the commandment of <em>maakeh</em>. There it is understood that the essential <em>maakeh</em> flows from the aspect of <span class="kt">Bina</span> [Understanding — the third <em>sefira</em>]. See there. And <em>Bina</em> is the aspect of <em>"the mother who spreads her shelter over the children"</em> — it emerges that <em>maakeh</em> is in the aspect of <em>sukkah</em>, as stated above.</p>

<div class="halacha-closing">
  Halacha 3 — in Hilchos Chovel B'chaveiro [Laws of One Who Injures His Fellow], Halacha 3.
  <br><em>Blessed is the Merciful One Who gave us a threefold Torah.</em>
</div>

<!-- TRANSLATOR SUMMARY -->
<div class="summary-box">
<h3>📜 Translator's Summary — Maakeh and Protection of the Soul, Halacha 2</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Sukkah = Intellect = Protection:</strong> The <em>sukkah</em> represents divine intellect — <em>Ima d'misachecha al banin</em> (the mother sheltering her children). A house can only truly be built when founded on this wisdom-dimension. This is Rebbe Nachman's teaching in Likutay Moharan I §266 on Yaakov building a house after Sukos.</li>
  <li><strong>The Maakeh as <em>Imitatio Dei</em>:</strong> Just as G‑d protects Israel through the <em>sukkah</em>-aspect (the Shechina spreading Her canopy), so too every Jew is commanded to actively protect others from harm. Fulfilling this commandment below directly arouses the same divine protection above.</li>
  <li><strong>Blood vs. Seichel:</strong> The dominance of blood (anger, animalistic drives, <em>ruach shtus</em>) is the polar opposite of <em>sukkah</em>-intellect. Blood corrupts the house; wisdom builds it.</li>
  <li><strong>The Fallen Sukkah of David:</strong> When any Jew falls or is harmed — physically or spiritually — the Shechina suffers and enters the aspect of the "fallen Sukkah of David" (Amos 9:11). Guarding others literally raises up the Shechina, fulfilling: <em>"I will raise up the fallen Sukkah of David."</em></li>
  <li><strong>Etz Chaim Confirmation:</strong> The Ari's <em>Sha'ar ABIY"A</em> locates the source of <em>maakeh</em> in <em>Bina</em> — the <em>sefira</em> of Understanding, the Divine Mother — directly confirming: <em>maakeh</em> = <em>sukkah</em>.</li>
</ul>
<div class="translator-label">— Translator's summary, for ajew.org</div>
